From 19a035a8c7dc9c33801d3f896fbff771b15db3eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:58:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): hand off model.options to a warm always-on
 successor [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: After an example gateway core rollover, Desktop
model.options stayed on the predecessor always-on :9149 and 503'd until a manual
pause-turns+SIGTERM. Successor :9148 had already begun serving.

Why 1: The client's existing TCP splice through :9147 stayed on :9149 — the
proxy routes only new connections (always_on_rollover.Proxy).
Why 2: :9149 was already superseded (core-stale logged busy, not left/live_ports)
so the roller had switched; retirement still required the idle fence
(web_server_skew_exit._run_retirement_watchdog).
Why 3: Unpausable turns refused fence.prepare; HTTP Connection: close drain does
not move the multiplexed WS that carries model.options RPC.
Why 4: core-stale pause-turns (180s) also refused rather than kill the turn;
the updater left the process to Desktop reconnect.
Root (happened): Blue/green converged process replacement, not control-plane
admission, so a busy predecessor could pin model.options indefinitely.
Root (not caught): Tests covered idle drain and fence refusal, not successor
serving + busy predecessor + model.options still on the old process.
Recurrence: same pattern Nov 12 (hermes-sync core_stale_serve_backends).

Countermeasures:
- symptom: GET /api/model/options and model.options RPC on a superseded always-on
  backend return the successor's payload (allowlisted control read only).
- root: no local picker build on stale modules; writes/prompts are not forwarded;
  missing successor still 503s; non-always-on ports never read live active.json.
- detection: tests/hermes_cli/test_always_on_control_handoff.py

Proof: hermes-core-wt test of the new file plus test_code_skew,
test_model_rpc_skew_guard, test_always_on_drain — 29 passed.
